      info_update: 'New versions', info_update_text: 'A copy bought from the seller asks once when it starts whether a newer version exists. That request carries nothing about you or your notes, and if there is one you only get a link: nothing installs by itself.',
      update_title: 'A new version is available: {version}', update_text: 'Veuly {version} is ready. Download it and replace the app; your notes stay where they are.', update_get: 'Download',
      info_ask: 'Asking your notes', info_ask__work: 'Asking your minutes',
      info_ask_text: 'On a course\'s Ask page, or on the home page, you can ask a question about your classes. {service} gets the question, a list of the classes with what each was about, and the parts of the notes, transcripts and files that match it, and answers only from them, with links to where each thing comes from. Nothing of it is kept, except the questions you save.',
      info_ask_text__work: 'On a project\'s Ask page, or on the home page, you can ask a question about your meetings. {service} gets the question, a list of the meetings with what each was about, and the parts of the minutes, transcripts and documents that match it, and answers only from them, with links to where each thing comes from. Nothing of it is kept, except the questions you save.',
      info_pages: 'Pages of your files in the notes', info_pages__work: 'Pages of your files in the minutes',
      info_pages_text: 'Your PDFs reach {service} as text. Veuly tells it which pages hold a figure, a chart or a photo, and when the class spent time on one, {service} can ask to show that page (six at most). Veuly then makes the picture from your own file, on this computer, and puts it in the note, with the file and the page under it, so it goes wherever the note goes: Obsidian, Confluence, the PDF. Published to Confluence through your Claude account, a picture is named and not shown, as any picture is. "Write it again" with a request sends those pictures to {service}, like the pictures of your notes. A PowerPoint file stays as text. You can turn this off in Course settings.',
      info_pages_text__work: 'Your PDFs reach {service} as text. Veuly tells it which pages hold a figure, a chart or a photo, and when the meeting spent time on one, {service} can ask to show that page (six at most). Veuly then makes the picture from your own file, on this computer, and puts it in the minutes, with the file and the page under it, so it goes wherever the minutes go: Obsidian, Confluence, the PDF. Published to Confluence through your Claude account, a picture is named and not shown, as any picture is. "Write it again" with a request sends those pictures to {service}, like the pictures of your notes. A PowerPoint file stays as text. You can turn this off in Project settings.',
      info_sync: 'A folder kept in step',
      info_sync_text: 'On a course’s settings page you can link folders on this computer, and their files come in by themselves when the app starts, when you open the course, before a note is written and about every 10 minutes. Veuly only reads those folders: it never changes anything there, and a file deleted from one stays in the course, marked, until you remove it. It waits while something records.',
      info_sync_text__work: 'On a project’s settings page you can link folders on this computer, and their files come in by themselves when the app starts, when you open the project, before the minutes are written and about every 10 minutes. Veuly only reads those folders: it never changes anything there, and a file deleted from one stays in the project, marked, until you remove it. It waits while something records.',
