      info_title: 'About Veuly',
      info_what: 'Veuly records a class, lets you type your own notes while the teacher talks, and writes one study note at the end, from the recording, your notes and the course files.',
      info_what__work: 'Veuly records a meeting, lets you type your own notes meanwhile, and writes the minutes at the end, from the recording, your notes and the project files.',
      info_how: 'How a class goes',
      info_how__work: 'How a meeting goes',
      info_step1: 'Open a course in the side panel and start a new class.',
      info_step1__work: 'Open a project in the side panel and start a new meeting.',
      info_step2: 'Type your notes while it records: each line keeps the moment you typed it. "{mute}" leaves out what should not be written down. Screenshots you take and photos you receive meanwhile go into the notes by themselves.',
      info_step3: 'Press "{finish}". The recording is turned into text on this computer, usually most of it already while it records, and {service} writes the note.',
      info_step3__work: 'Press "{finish}". The recording is turned into text on this computer, usually most of it already while it records, and {service} writes the minutes.',
      info_step4: 'Read the result, edit it if you want, send it by e-mail, and find it later on the home page or on its course\'s page, which lists every class.',
