      key_finish: 'finish the class (it asks first)', key_finish__work: 'finish the meeting (it asks first)', key_tabs: 'open {a}, {b} or {c}', key_save: 'save now',
      info_privacy: 'What leaves this computer',
      info_privacy_text: 'The recording is turned into text here and is not sent anywhere. As soon as any text exists the recording is deleted, even before the note is written. With no text at all it stays so you can try again: Veuly itself transcribes it once more, on this computer and with no AI, when it next starts or after 24 hours, even if it was closed or asleep all that time. If that gives no text it is deleted then, and the page says so. Veuly keeps no audio. What goes to {service} to write it: the transcript, your notes with their images, and the text of the files you added. If you link a Claude project and choose to send notes to it, the final notes are also copied into that project. If you switch on the Obsidian agent, Claude Code also reads and edits files of your vault, by the rules you wrote there.',
      info_privacy_claude: '{service} also gets the title, date, length and language of the class, and your name if you gave it in Settings. Claude Code is started so that it keeps no copy of the conversation on this computer, and so is Codex.',
